{"changes":["cmd/telemetry.go: `eka telemetry list [--session \u003cid\u003e] [--repo \u003cid\u003e] [--since \u003ct\u003e] [--until \u003ct\u003e] [--json]` streams the session files with bufio (the whole set is never held in memory), validates the chain and the record version (v must equal 1), sorts by session file (each file is in seq order) so the (sessionId, seq) order holds, and applies the repo/period filters on `at` (informational only, never an ordering key). A malformed line, a broken chain or an unsupported version is a deterministic error naming file:line.","--json emits one canonical record object per line (JSONL), byte-identical across runs for a fixed file state. A missing telemetry directory is an empty result (exit 0)."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Implemented the `eka telemetry list` read side (WI-B): a streaming, deterministic query over the append-only stream sorted by (sessionId, seq), with --session/--repo/--since/--until filters and --json (JSONL), plus record-version and chain validation.","tests":["go test ./cmd/ -run 'Telemetry.*List' -count=1 -\u003e ok.","TestTelemetryListJSONStableAndOrdered: two --json runs are byte-identical and ordered (aaa/0, bbb/0, bbb/1).","TestTelemetryListFilters: --repo/--since/--until filter deterministically; a malformed --since exits 2.","TestTelemetryListMalformed: a malformed line exits 1 with file:line; non-vacuous (a clean file exits 0).","TestTelemetryListUnsupportedVersion: a hand-written v:2 line exits 1 ('unsupported version 2', path:1); non-vacuous.","TestTelemetryListUnattributedFile: an unattributed session file (name .jsonl) is discovered via os.ReadDir and both record lines are printed.","gofmt/vet/build clean; go test -timeout 1200s ./cmd/... ok."]}